# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# torch.Tensor.to complex-cast-on-gcu shim (torch_gcu P21 defect workaround)
#
# torch_gcu's topsatenCopy aborts the whole process for on-device casts whose
# source or target dtype is complex (int/float <-> complex), which kills the
# accuracy suite during input construction (`indices.to(torch.complex64)`)
# before this op ever runs. Complex tensors themselves are usable on gcu once
# created (CPU<->GCU transfers of complex data are plain copies), so route
# complex-target casts through CPU and land the result on the caller's target
# device. Every other call shape (non-complex dtype, cpu source, explicit
# device-only moves) passes through to the original implementation untouched.
# Narrow, value-preserving, and safe to drop once topsatenCopy supports
# complex dtypes. Same pattern as add.py's complex randn/isclose shims;
# per-call device check keeps real-CUDA hosts on the native path.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
